  "hypothesis": "The two-stage attack this repository cites - an unsteckered sweep scored by index of coincidence, then a stecker hill-climb - is usable on 1941-09-30 traffic of 97 to 167 letters carrying a ten-pair stecker. Concretely: the true rotor setting's unsteckered IC will stand at least three standard deviations above the wrong-setting null at the target length and stecker size; the stecker hill-climb will recover a known ten-pair plugboard and its plaintext exactly at those lengths; a truncated climb will separate the true setting well enough to serve as a cheap pre-filter; and the indicator-coupled formulation phase1.py implements will be hill-climbable.",
  "refuted_by": "Any of the four clauses failing at the target scale: an IC z-score below the declared usable threshold at 167 letters with ten pairs; failure to recover a known plugboard or plaintext exactly; no truncated climb separating the true setting; or the indicator-coupled climb failing to recover the true message keys when handed the true wheel order and ring setting.",
